-> Commands:
clear        clear the environment
env          browse through the environment
exit         quit
?            display this help info
$var = 'expr augment the environment
$var = expr  eval and assign
expr         evaluate the expression

where expr could be any of the following:

EXP -> BINARY-EXP (EXP1,EXP2)
     | UNARY-EXP (EXP)
     | EXP1 OP EXP2

BINARY-EXP -> add | sub | mul | div | equ
            | ne  | lt  | gt | lte | gte

UNARY-EXP -> sqrt | real | rat 

VAR -> a variable name

-> 
-> Set $a to 50+51
-> 53
-> Eval	$a+49
Set	$a to 54
-> $a	54
$prec	1598

-> 1571
-> 1598
